  "claims_zeron": {
    "about": "A name or description may not say the plugin is Zeron's own unless its publisher is (the maintainer badge). Folded as mark_claims folds (ignorables gone), U+2019 and U+02BC read as an apostrophe, each run of separators (White_Space, U+FEFF, General_Category P*) but the apostrophe read as one space, it says any of phrases whole (no ASCII letter or digit right before or after it). The edge refuses a publish 400 claims_zeron unless the publisher carries maintainer; a device, which can't know the publisher, gives the warning claims_zeron on that field. The listing cases named 'claims_zeron:' hold both sides to it (warnings).",
    "phrases": [
      "by zeron",
      "from zeron",
      "zeron team",
      "zeron's own",
      "zeron approved",
      "zeron certified",
      "zeron endorsed",
      "zeron recommended",
      "zeron staff"
    ]
  },
  "consent": {
    "about": "A program's name is lowercased and loses one Windows extension (windows_extensions) before it's looked up. It can do anything you can unless it's in contained. It gives full control when it's in full_control, as it is or with its trailing digits and dots taken off (python3.12 → python). commands_anything is every program that can do anything you can and is neither full_control nor held_to_its_own_rules. A host is local when it's localhost, a private or loopback address, ends .localhost .local .internal .lan .home.arpa .intranet .corp, has one label, or ends in a number (decimal or 0x hex); network_local is every host but * that is local, network_named every host that names one host exactly (not * or *.…) and isn't local.",
